  "id": "champion-road-2000",
  "name": "Champion Road 2000",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Champion Road 2000, the tournament series that closed Japan's Grand Party 1999-2000 season, ran from 9 January to 20 February 2000, with its final on 26 February. It began a month before Neo Genesis came out on 4 February 2000, and its venues were where many players first tried the new set's cards. At the 3-player Win Corner, one of the side events, the first 100 players to win three games in a row received Berry and Miracle Berry, the Neo Genesis cards with Champion Road 2000 (チャンピオンロード2000) printed in place of the set symbol and rarity mark. Neo Genesis' Chikorita, Cyndaquil and Totodile also exist with a Champion Road stamp.",
